{"availability":"available","full":"dguywhoknows/crossword-generator","name":"crossword-generator","description":"Pick any theme: AI writes the words and clues, a backtracking-style constructor builds the grid, and you solve it in the browser.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-07T04:21:36Z","updated":"2026-10-10T03:50:58Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/crossword-generator/","topics":["crossword","game","github-pages","javascript","puzzle"],"demo":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/crossword-generator/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.292Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.292Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.292Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.292Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Pick any theme: AI writes the words and clues, a backtracking-style constructor builds the grid, and you solve it in the browser.","Type a theme (\"Space exploration\", \"90s cartoons\", \"Your best friend's hobbies\") and choose a clue style. The AI writes about 18 themed answers with clues, from easy definitions to punny misdirection. A local constructor then interlocks them: it tries dozens of orderings, scores every legal crossing (no illegal side-by-side letters, proper word boundaries), and keeps the densest, squarest layout before numbering it in standard reading order. The solving UI behaves like a real crossword app, with arrow keys, Tab/Shift+Tab between clues, Space to switch direction, Backspace, a live clue bar,…"],"features":["AI-written themed answers + clues in three styles (easy, NYT-Tuesday, punny/tricky)","Grid constructor: multi-attempt search, crossing validation, adjacency rules, area/squareness scoring","Standard numbering, across/down clue lists with completion strike-through","Full keyboard solving: arrows, Tab/Shift+Tab, Space to flip dire